15. (Currently amended) A method for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers in a computer network for sending data to a client computer, the method comprising the steps of:

accessing a server computer through a path in a computer network, the path including one or more server computers;

adding information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, wherein the information is __dynamically determined based on real-time server load metrics and network latency measurements__;

the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier; and

selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator, __wherein the selection is performed by a media request broker that analyzes the real-time server load metrics and network latency measurements to determine optimal server selection__.

16. (Currently amended) The method of claim 15, __wherein the second server computer is a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature that is dynamically generated and embedded within the hyperlink, the method further comprising the steps of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an HTTP request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this HTTP request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, wherein the unique signature is transmitted to a media request broker that selects the first server computer based on analysis of the unique signature and associated server load information__.

