18. (Currently amended) The method of claim 17, __wherein the media request broker selects the first server computer based on the information by analyzing real-time server performance metrics including processor utilization, memory availability, and network bandwidth capacity__.

24. (Currently amended) A system for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers in a computer network for sending data to a client computer, the system comprising:

a client computer;

a plurality of server computers including a first server computer and a second server computer;

a network path connecting the client computer to the plurality of server computers;

a media request broker configured to __dynamically determine server selection based on real-time server load metrics and network latency measurements, wherein the media request broker adds information indicative of at least one server computer to a locator of a resource on the second server computer, the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier, and selects the first server computer based on the information added to the locator__.

